{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 30, :comments ["<b>How could one pursue.</b> One may explain it as a wakeup call to the nations, who do not awaken with a stirring wakeup call, which is ״אֵיכָה יִרְדֹּף אֶחָד״ etc. — meaning, one of the nations pursuing a thousand of Israel. The meaning is that in all ordinary wars among the nations nothing like this is to be found, for no enemy among the nations attains such power and might." "<b>How could one pursue a thousand.</b> Meaning, one singled out from the nations pursuing a thousand of Israel, etc. And see what I explained in parashat Bechukotai on the verse (Leviticus 26:8) ״וְרָדְפוּ מִכֶּם חֲמִשָּׁה מֵאָה״ etc." "<b>Were it not that their Rock.</b> Meaning the attribute of justice, as I explained on the verse (Deuteronomy 32:4) ״הַצּוּר תָּמִים״ etc. And His saying ״וַה׳ הִסְגִּירָם״ — meaning the attribute of mercy together with the attribute of justice, for without this there would not have been such a decline for Israel that a thousand would fall before one."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:21:32.887801578Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}